    [v0.31.0rc][BugFix][MRV2] Skip non-Tensor KV cache components in block zeroer (#19696)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Backport #19598 to `releases/v0.31.0rc`.
    
    Skip non-Tensor components before calling `numel()` in the MRV2 KV block
    zeroer, avoiding initialization errors for nested tuple/list cache
    bindings while retaining empty-Tensor filtering. Original comments are
    unchanged.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Avoids the tuple/list `numel` exception while preserving zeroing of
    nonempty Tensor components. Nested containers remain excluded; this
    change does not unwrap them.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `git diff --check` and Python AST syntax check passed. The code change
    matches #19598 exactly.
    - A3-560T Nightly passed for `DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-W8A8-DSpark-PCP`
    ([run](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40072129683))
    and `DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-w8a8-PD-MRV2`
    ([run](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40072148823)).
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
